<node id="KnowledgeGraph">
  <data key="d0">KnowledgeGraph</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The KnowledgeGraph is a conceptual system, structure, method, or framework primarily designed for organizing and representing information or knowledge. It is consistently managed, implemented, and indexed within the Obsidian environment.

This system is utilized to structure and store documentation and details across various categories. These categories explicitly include People, Projects, Topics, Documents, and Decisions. Specific examples of entities or entries it encompasses are 'Session Major', the 'Research Dashboard' (identified as a person), and the 'AI Research Dashboard' (identified as a project). The organization and representation of information within the KnowledgeGraph are also evident through its file paths, indicating a structured approach to knowledge management.&lt;SEP&gt;KnowledgeGraph is a system or conceptual framework being used or developed, which contains information about individuals like 'Not Started' and discussion topics.&lt;SEP&gt;KnowledgeGraph is a system or project mentioned in file paths, indicating its role in organizing information about people, projects, and action items within Obsidian.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ffee7e99a39b11f6d9d6277ba5594d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6af547d3e45d8ad51a44b6437545d4bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a2626ac3c4b4db2e1bb9274c8b58fa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576fa1ed41557cc09379e9532cd8fc48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57ca52f28d5bc68f21ab7c9caf670243&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea5150e6fca2cc266a2614914dfb7239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd7088becf52bb8a5c2ed784265260d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbbf68c07d5785152cb568cb44c097d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7347a0c6ac17d9cb58ce4f8eb857eb12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771986aa17685fe6999e419c1c67ae69</data>
